Detention ends at 3:40. Today it doesn't. You're the last student in Lincoln High when the vice principal comes over the speaker: stay in your rooms, lock your doors, don't open them for anyone. Even if you know them.

We follow you day by day through 30 days locked inside a school during a zombie outbreak: a teacher who keeps knocking, a bell that won't stop ringing, a kitchen raid, a gym full of the dead, a V painted on the football field at night, and a friendly voice on the PA that always knows where you are.

Real facts in this story: about a gallon of water per person per day; a water heater is a tank of tap water you can drain in an emergency; rooms built for more than 50 people need doors that swing outward; to a pilot, a V on the ground means "we need help", an X means "we need a doctor", and rocking the wings means "message received".

